      CEE 6410 - Engineering Systems Analysis
      Example 2.1 from Bishop Et Al Text (https://digitalcommons.usu.edu/ecstatic_all/76/)
      Modifies Example to add a labor constraint
       
      THE PROBLEM:
       
      A cr manufacturer makes coups and vans. The data are as follows:
       
      Yearly Resource
      Inputs or Profit      Months
      Availability
                           June             July           August            Return ($/acre)
      Hay                  2                1              1                 100
      Grain                1                2              0                 120
       
       
                      Determine the optimal water allocation plan.
       
      THE SOLUTION:
      Uses General Algebraic Modeling System to Solve this Linear Program
       
      Maddie Witte
      maddie.witte@usu.edu
      October 2, 2026
       
       
  29   
  30  * 1. DEFINE the SETS
  31  SETS crop /Hay, Grain/
  32       month /June, July, August/;
  33   
  34  * 2. DEFINE input data
  35  PARAMETERS
  36     c(crop) Objective function coefficients ($ per acre crop)
  37           /Hay 100,
  38          Grain 120 /
  39   
  40     b(month) Right hand constraint values (available water per month)
  41            /June 14000,
  42             July  18000,
  43             August  6000/;
  44   
  45  TABLE A(crop,month) Left hand side constraint coefficients: water per crop per month
  46                   June      July      August
  47   Hay             2         1         1
  48   Grain           1         2         0;
  49   
  50   
  51  * 3. DEFINE the variables
  52  VARIABLES X(crop) area planted (acres)
  53            VPROFIT  total profit ($);
  54   
  55  * Non-negativity constraints
  56  POSITIVE VARIABLES X;
  57   
  58  * 4. COMBINE variables and data in equations
  59  EQUATIONS
  60     PROFIT Total profit ($) and objective function value
  61     RES_CONSTRAIN(month) Resource Constraints
  62     MAX_AREA total amount of area the crops can fill;
  63   
  64  PROFIT..                   VPROFIT =E= SUM(crop, c(crop)*X(crop));
  65  RES_CONSTRAIN(month) ..    SUM(crop, A(crop,month)*X(crop)) =L= b(month);
  66  MAX_AREA..                 X(crop) =L= 10000;
****                                   $149
**** 149  Uncontrolled set entered as constant
  67   
  68  * 5. DEFINE the MODEL from the EQUATIONS
  69  MODEL PLANTING /PROFIT, RES_CONSTRAIN, MAX_AREA/;
  70  *Altnerative way to write (include all previously defined equations)
  71  *MODEL MAKING /ALL/;
  72   
  73   
  74  * 6. SOLVE the MODEL
  75  * Solve the MAKING model using a Linear Programming Solver (see File=>Options=>Solvers)
  76  *     to maximize VPROFIT
  77  SOLVE PLANTING USING LP MAXIMIZING VPROFIT;
****                                            $257
**** 257  Solve statement not checked because of previous errors
  78   
  79   
